@@ -39,22 +39,39 @@ Running locally requires API keys and a backend/frontend setup. The app has a Re
 
 ### API keys
 
-You need **at least one** model provider key (OpenAI, Anthropic, or Gemini).
-**Gemini and Replicate are strongly recommended for the best quality of
-screenshot-to-code accuracy** — Gemini powers asset extraction (reusing the
-real logos/images from your screenshot) and Replicate powers image
-generation, background removal, and image editing. Adding all four keys gives
-the best results and lets you compare multiple models per generation.
+All LLM calls (GPT, Claude, and Gemini variants) go through Ramp's Router
+(`https://api.router.com/v1`), which holds the provider credentials. The app
+only needs a Router key — do not configure OpenAI, Anthropic, or Gemini API
+keys. Replicate (image generation/editing) is not an LLM provider and is
+configured separately.
 
 | Key | Required? | What it unlocks |
 |-----|-----------|-----------------|
-| `OPENAI_API_KEY` | One of these three | GPT code-gen variants (GPT-5.5, GPT-5.4 Mini) |
-| `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` | One of these three | Claude code-gen variants (Opus 5, Opus 4.8, Fable 5, Sonnet 4.6) |
-| `GEMINI_API_KEY` | One of these three — **strongly recommended** | Gemini code-gen variants (3 Flash, 3.1 Pro); extracts real assets from the screenshot; required for video mode |
+| `RAMP_ROUTER_API_KEY` | **Required** | All code-gen variants (GPT, Claude, Gemini) via Router |
+| `ROUTER_MODEL_<NAME>` | **Required** for each model the app uses | Maps an internal model name to your account's Router model ID (see below) |
+| `ROUTER_PROVIDER_TIMEOUT` / `ROUTER_TIMEOUT_BEFORE_HEADERS` | Optional | Router per-provider-call timeout / time to first streaming event, in seconds |
 | `REPLICATE_API_KEY` | **Strongly recommended** | Image editing, background removal, and Replicate-backed image generation — without it, `edit_images` and `remove_backgrounds` are unavailable |
 
-With more keys, the app automatically picks a stronger mix of models per
-variant; with a single key it uses that provider's models only.
+Router model IDs are account-specific: list them with `GET /v1/models`
+(`curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $RAMP_ROUTER_API_KEY" https://api.router.com/v1/models`)
+and set one env var per internal model name. The env var name is
+`ROUTER_MODEL_` + the internal name upper-cased with non-alphanumerics
+replaced by `_`. The default variant sets use:
+
+- `ROUTER_MODEL_GPT_5_6_SOL`, `ROUTER_MODEL_GPT_6_1_SOL`
+- `ROUTER_MODEL_CLAUDE_OPUS_5`, `ROUTER_MODEL_CLAUDE_OPUS_5_5`
+- `ROUTER_MODEL_GEMINI_3_FLASH_PREVIEW`, `ROUTER_MODEL_GEMINI_3_1_PRO_PREVIEW`
+
+Other selectable models follow the same pattern (e.g. `ROUTER_MODEL_GPT_5_5`,
+`ROUTER_MODEL_GPT_5_4_MINI`, `ROUTER_MODEL_GPT_5_4_2026_03_05`,
+`ROUTER_MODEL_GPT_5_6_TERRA`, `ROUTER_MODEL_CLAUDE_OPUS_4_8`,
+`ROUTER_MODEL_CLAUDE_FABLE_5`, `ROUTER_MODEL_CLAUDE_SONNET_4_6`,
+`ROUTER_MODEL_GEMINI_3_5_FLASH`, `ROUTER_MODEL_GEMINI_3_6_FLASH`). Pick
+models that support image input — screenshots are sent as images.
+
+Not available through Router: **video mode** (needs Gemini-native video
+input) and the **asset extraction** tool (needs Gemini-native bounding-box
+detection). Video mode reports an error; asset extraction is not offered.
 
 If you'd like to run the app with Ollama open-source models (not recommended due to poor-quality results), [follow this comment](https://github.com/abi/screenshot-to-code/issues/354#issuecomment-2435479853).
 
